                "In a blender, combine the soaked cashews with 1 cup of the coconut milk. Blend on high for at least 2 minutes, until completely smooth with no gritty flecks remaining.",
                "In a saucepan, combine the cashew cream, remaining coconut milk, sugar, and salt. Warm over medium heat, stirring often, until the sugar fully dissolves. Do not let it boil.",
                "Remove from heat and whisk in the vanilla extract, vodka (if using), and guar gum (if using), whisking briskly so the guar gum disperses evenly instead of clumping.",
                "Pour the base into a container, cover, and chill in the refrigerator for at least 4 hours or overnight.",
                "Churn the cold base in an ice cream maker according to the manufacturer's instructions, about 20-30 minutes, until it thickens to soft-serve consistency.",
                "Transfer to a freezer-safe container, press a piece of parchment or plastic wrap directly onto the surface, and freeze for at least 4 hours until firm.",
