                "Blue cheese and other crumbly varieties tend to hold up better than soft cheeses since they're already lower in moisture.",
                "Skip freezing cheese you plan to serve fresh on a platter; the crumbly, drier texture after thawing is much more noticeable when the cheese isn't melted or mixed into a dish.",
